INT. CITY BANK - SUBTERRANEAN VAULT - NIGHT

A cathedral of steel. Rows of safe-deposit boxes climb the walls, thousands of little brass doors. Cold light from a single emergency strip. The great round door stands ajar, its locking bolts retracted like the fingers of a sleeper.

Empty. Silent. A single security camera turns on its bracket and finds nothing.

A footfall on the stairs. Another. Then the quiet scrape of a crowbar being laid down.

SABINE ARROWOOD, forties, enters in a black jumpsuit, gloves tucked in her belt, a canvas bag over one shoulder. Dark hair under a cap. She pauses at the door, looks at the open bolts, and smiles slightly as if at a private joke.

SABINE
(low)
Sloppy.

She crosses the vault, runs a gloved finger along the boxes. Stops at number 4417. She reaches into her bag and takes out a small recorder. She clicks it on.

SABINE (V.O.)
(from the recorder, her own voice, recorded days ago)
"If you're hearing this, Sabine, the door will be open, and the box will be empty. Don't panic. That's the plan."

Sabine stares at the recorder. Her smile fades. She clicks it off. She slides the key into 4417. Turns. The door swings open. Nothing inside but a folded note.

She unfolds it. Reads.

SABINE (CONT'D)
(softly)
Clever girl.

She pockets the note, shoulders the bag, and strides to the open vault door. Alarms stay silent. She pauses at the threshold, glances back at the shining wall of boxes, and shuts the great door behind her.
